\fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Lets you specify the kind of frame that borders the image . The possible styles are:\
\fs14\
\pard \s6 \li1810 \fi-298 \ri1007 \ql \tx1810 \tx3376 \tx3753 \fs28 \'b7\tab NSImageFrameNone\'d0an invisible frame\
\'b7\tab NSImageFramePhoto\'d0a thin black outline and a dropped shadow\
\'b7\tab NSImageFrameGrayBezel\'d0a gray, concave bezel that makes the image look sunken\
\'b7\tab NSImageGroove\'d0a thin groove that looks etched around the image\
\'b7\tab NSImageFrameButton\'d0a convex bezel that makes the image stand out in relief, like a button\
\fs14\
