\fs14\
\fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Lets you specify the way that the image alters to fit the frame. The possible values are:\
\fs14\
\pard \s5 \li1810 \fi-298 \ri1007 \ql \tx1810 \tx6300 \tx6590 \tx15154 \fs28 \'b7\tab NSScaleProportionally. If the image is too large, it shrinks to fit inside the frame. If the image is too small, it expands. The proportions of the image are preserved.\
\fs14\
\fs28 \'b7\tab NSScaleToFit. The image shrinks or expands, and its proportions distort, until it exactly fits the frame.\
\fs14\
\fs28 \'b7\tab NSScaleNone. The size and proportions of the image don\'27t change. If the frame is too small to display the whole image, the edges of the image are trimmed off.\
\fs14\
\pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 \fs28 The default \i scaling\i0  is NSScaleProportionally.\
\fs14\
